From 681b0998edceb70e492c548ee569321bcbd3ddb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duchil6063 <duchil6063@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:35:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] i18n: built-in Korean UI, language setting, Korean
 default

Every user-facing string goes through gui::i18n::t(), a lookup into a
built-in English->Korean table (src/gui/i18n.cpp). Unknown strings pass
through unchanged, so partial coverage degrades to English rather than
losing text. Engine/fill error sentences are translated at the point
they surface, so the fill sources stay untouched.

The language lives in QSettings ui/language ("ko" default, "en") with
a combo on the settings dialog's General page; a change restarts the
editor, reusing the icon-set restart path. Qt's own dialog strings
(OK/Cancel, color dialog) come from qtbase_ko.qm, loaded from
translations/ next to the executable when Korean is active.

Names that double as data stay functional: tool ids, settings keys and
livery section names are never translated; the shapes-browser Custom
category was renamed to "Custom Groups" so it no longer collides with
the settings dialog's "Custom" color mode; vinyl catalog categories are
translated once where they enter, so display and lookups agree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
